IMPORT prelude

-- Public Utilities Act 2001 (Singapore) -- my water supply: whether I am a consumer and an occupier, when the Board may cut off my
-- supply and what I must do to have it resumed, how much notice I must be given before the Board's people enter my premises, what
-- I can recover from the Board when my supply fails or its works affect me, what may be done to my goods for an unpaid bill, my
-- duty to report a wasting pipe and to answer for a supply reinstated without authority, and my claim for a refund of an overpaid
-- bill.
--
-- SEAT: the consumer -- the person "who is supplied with water or whose premises are for the time being connected for the purpose
-- of a supply of water" (s 2), usually the owner or occupier of the premises, to whom the Board's powers of supply, cut-off, entry
-- and recovery are applied.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("consumer", "occupier"); ss 21(3), (5); 22(3), (4); 23(1) to (3); 24(1) to (3); 24A(2), (3), (7); 24B(1);
-- 25(1), (2), (6) to (8); 27(2); 28; 31(1), (3); 32(2); 34; 37; 38(2); 55B(1); 68B.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 29 May 2026 (amendments to Act 8 of 2026 shown), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PUA2001.txt. Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit; the arrangement of
-- sections printed at its head is displaced against the body from about s 24 onwards.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: tariffs, the waterborne tax and the water conservation tax (ss 20, 20A) -- their amounts are set by orders not
-- deposited; the late payment charge (s 35), whose amount is prescribed by the Board and not deposited; the conditions of supply
-- (s 21(1), (2), (4)); security on first supply (s 22(1), (2)); the Board's powers to relocate its own installations, to require
-- removal of obstructions and to stop or reduce supply (ss 26, 27(1), 28 beyond the abatement, 33) other than as they set my
-- remedies; Part 3A compensation for temporary occupation and owner-initiated acquisition (ss 40A to 40F); s 36 contributions;
-- s 68A procedure. The fee "prescribed" for a s 25 notice is not deposited and is not computed.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the individual's seat, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC
-- USE AS ADVICE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Utilities Act 2001 -- my water supply`

§§ `s 2 -- am I a consumer, am I the occupier`

-- s 2: "consumer" means "a person who is supplied with water or whose premises are for the time being connected for the purpose
-- of a supply of water with any system of supply". "occupier" means "the person in occupation of any premises and includes the
-- person having the charge, management or control of the premises either on the person's own account or as agent of another
-- person, but does not include a lodger".
DECLARE `My place` HAS
    `I am supplied with water`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `my premises are connected to a system of water supply`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am in occupation of the premises`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have the charge, management or control of the premises`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- on my own account or as agent
    `I am a lodger`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN   -- borrowed term, asked as a fact

GIVEN `the place` IS A `My place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a consumer` IF
        `the place`'s `I am supplied with water`
    OR  `the place`'s `my premises are connected to a system of water supply`

GIVEN `the place` IS A `My place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I the occupier` IF
        (   `the place`'s `I am in occupation of the premises`
         OR `the place`'s `I have the charge, management or control of the premises`)
    AND NOT `the place`'s `I am a lodger`

§§ `ss 21(3), 22(3), 23, 34(2) -- may the Board cut off my supply`

-- s 21(3): the Board "may refuse to give, or may discontinue, a supply of water to any premises which -- (a) has been erected in
-- contravention of any written law; (b) is in a ruinous or dangerous condition; or (c) has a water service installation that is in
-- an unsatisfactory condition".
-- s 22(3): where security has not been given or has become invalid or insufficient, "(a) the Board may by notice require that
-- person, within 7 days after the service of the notice, to give the Board reasonable security ... and (b) if that person fails to
-- give the security, the Board may if it thinks fit discontinue the supply for so long as the failure continues".
-- s 23(1): if a person entitled to a supply under an agreement "makes default in payment of any sum payable", the Board "may
-- discontinue the supply ... until any sum payable under the agreement together with the expenses ... are fully paid".
-- s 23(2): "If, in the opinion of the Board, any person is responsible for the misuse or waste of any water", the Board may give
-- written notice to discontinue it within a period, "and, if the misuse or waste continues after the expiry of that period, the
-- Board may discontinue the supply".
-- s 34(2): an occupier who neglects to report a pipe wasting water -- "the supply may be summarily discontinued by the order of the
-- Board until the necessary repairs are effected".
-- Each power is the Board's ("may"), so the answer is that the Board MAY cut off the supply, never that it will. The Board's
-- opinion in s 23(2) is asked as a fact. Day 7 after service is taken as still in time (an inference: the text does not say whether
-- the day of service counts).
DECLARE `My supply` HAS
    `my premises were erected in breach of written law or are ruinous or dangerous`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 21(3)(a), (b)
    `my water service installation is in an unsatisfactory condition`                IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 21(3)(c)
    `the Board served me a notice to give security`                                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 22(3)(a)
    `days since the security notice was served`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `I have given the security`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am in default in paying a sum due under my supply agreement`                  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 23(1)
    `the Board is of the opinion that I am responsible for misuse or waste of water` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 23(2), the Board's judgment
    `the Board gave me written notice to stop the misuse or waste`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the misuse or waste continued after the period in that notice`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `I neglected to report a pipe wasting water and it is not yet repaired`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 34(2)

DECLARE `Cut-off position` IS ONE OF
    `the Board may cut off my supply, if it thinks fit`
    `ss 21, 22, 23 and 34 give the Board no ground to cut off my supply`

GIVEN `the supply` IS A `My supply`
GIVETH A `Cut-off position`
DECIDE `May the Board cut off my supply` IS
    IF      `the premises ground under s 21(3)`
         OR `the security ground under s 22(3)`
         OR `the supply`'s `I am in default in paying a sum due under my supply agreement`
         OR `the misuse ground under s 23(2)`
         OR `the supply`'s `I neglected to report a pipe wasting water and it is not yet repaired`
    THEN `the Board may cut off my supply, if it thinks fit`
    ELSE `ss 21, 22, 23 and 34 give the Board no ground to cut off my supply`
  WHERE
    `the premises ground under s 21(3)` MEANS
            `the supply`'s `my premises were erected in breach of written law or are ruinous or dangerous`
        OR  `the supply`'s `my water service installation is in an unsatisfactory condition`
    `the security ground under s 22(3)` MEANS
            `the supply`'s `the Board served me a notice to give security`
        AND `the supply`'s `days since the security notice was served` GREATER THAN 7
        AND NOT `the supply`'s `I have given the security`
    `the misuse ground under s 23(2)` MEANS
            `the supply`'s `the Board is of the opinion that I am responsible for misuse or waste of water`
        AND `the supply`'s `the Board gave me written notice to stop the misuse or waste`
        AND `the supply`'s `the misuse or waste continued after the period in that notice`

-- s 37(2): "Where the Board has discontinued the supply of water to any premises under this Act, the Board may resume the supply
-- within a reasonable time if the person in default -- (a) has made good the default; and (b) has paid the reasonable expenses of
-- disconnecting and re-connecting the supply." Both are needed; even then resumption is the Board's ("may").
GIVEN `I have made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN, `I have paid the reasonable expenses of disconnecting and reconnecting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what s 37(2) asks before my supply may be resumed` IF
    `I have made good the default` AND `I have paid the reasonable expenses of disconnecting and reconnecting`

§§ `ss 24, 24A, 24B, 31, 32, 55B -- how much notice I must be given before the Board enters`

-- s 24(1): the Board may enter "any premises at all reasonable hours in the day or night, or at any other time that may be agreed
-- with the owner or occupier" to survey, inspect or execute authorised work. (2): it "must not ... enter any dwelling house in
-- actual occupation, except with the consent of the occupier of the house, without 6 hours' previous notice to the occupier".
-- (3): premises of a class the Minister declares liable to inspection may be entered "at any time of the day or night and without
-- notice ... using such force as may be necessary".
-- s 24A(3): to lay pipes, meters or installations the Board "must not enter any premises ... unless the Board has given at least
-- 14 days' written notice of intention to enter to every owner and occupier".
-- s 31(1): to examine, repair or remove its pipes and meters, or to ascertain the water used -- "at all reasonable hours ... or at
-- any other time that may be agreed"; no notice is stated.
-- s 32(2): to enter premises within 100 metres of its works, "at least 7 days' written notice".
-- s 24B(1): "Despite anything in section 24, 24A, 31, 32 or 33, where the Board considers that immediate action is necessary" (an
-- emergency, fire or excessive drought; water quality; repairs; supply to consumers; conservation; public safety) it "may
-- immediately and without notice enter any premises".
-- s 55B(1): an authorised officer "may, at any time without notice, enter any premises" to check compliance or investigate an
-- offence.
DECLARE `Why the Board is entering` IS ONE OF
    `to survey, inspect or execute authorised work`                       -- s 24
    `to lay or install mains, pipes, meters or water installations`       -- s 24A
    `to examine, repair or remove its pipes and meters`                   -- s 31(1)
    `to work on premises within 100 metres of its works`                  -- s 32
    `to check compliance or investigate an offence`                       -- s 55B

DECLARE `The entry` HAS
    `why`                                                                      IS A `Why the Board is entering`
    `my premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy`                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 24(2)
    `I consent to the entry`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 24(2)
    `the Minister has declared my class of premises liable to inspection at any time` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 24(3)
    `the Board considers immediate action necessary for a s 24B reason`        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 24B, the Board's judgment

DECLARE `Notice I must be given` IS ONE OF
    `none: the Board may enter immediately and without notice`
    `none stated: entry at reasonable hours or at a time agreed with me`
    `at least 6 hours' notice, unless I consent`
    `at least 7 days' written notice`
    `at least 14 days' written notice`

GIVEN `the entry` IS A `The entry`
GIVETH A `Notice I must be given`
DECIDE `How much notice must I be given before the Board enters my premises` IS
    CONSIDER `the entry`'s `why`
    WHEN `to check compliance or investigate an offence` THEN `none: the Board may enter immediately and without notice`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the entry`'s `the Board considers immediate action necessary for a s 24B reason`
        THEN `none: the Board may enter immediately and without notice`
        ELSE
            CONSIDER `the entry`'s `why`
            WHEN `to survey, inspect or execute authorised work` THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF `the entry`'s `the Minister has declared my class of premises liable to inspection at any time`
                        THEN `none: the Board may enter immediately and without notice`
                    IF `the entry`'s `my premises are a dwelling house I actually occupy` AND NOT `the entry`'s `I consent to the entry`
                        THEN `at least 6 hours' notice, unless I consent`
                    OTHERWISE `none stated: entry at reasonable hours or at a time agreed with me`
            WHEN `to lay or install mains, pipes, meters or water installations` THEN `at least 14 days' written notice`
            WHEN `to work on premises within 100 metres of its works` THEN `at least 7 days' written notice`
            OTHERWISE `none stated: entry at reasonable hours or at a time agreed with me`

§§ `ss 21(5), 22(4), 23(3), 24(1), 24A(2), (7), 27(2), 28, 31(3), 38(2) -- what I can recover from the Board`

-- s 27(2): "The Board shall not be liable in respect of any loss or damage caused to any person by reason of -- (a) any failure to
-- provide or delay in providing any supply of water ...; or (b) any failure, interruption, suspension or restriction of any supply
-- of water." ss 21(5), 22(4), 23(3): the Board "shall not be liable for any loss or damage" caused by a refusal or discontinuance
-- under those sections. ss 24(1), 31(3): no "fee, charge or expense" on account of entry.
-- s 28: the Board may reduce the quantity supplied "without incurring any liability for so doing other than the liability to make
-- a proportionate abatement in the sum agreed to be paid for the supply of water".
-- s 38(2): "The Board must make reasonable compensation to any person who suffers damage by reason of" ways, watercourses, drains
-- and channels "interrupted, damaged or rendered useless" by its works.
-- s 24A(7): "Any costs and expenses reasonably incurred by the owner, supplier or occupier in complying with any notice under
-- subsection (5) or (6) must be borne by the Board."
-- s 24A(2): "Except as provided under Part 3A", no fee, charge or expense for entry under s 24A. Part 3A (compensation for temporary
-- occupation) is NOT ENCODED, so for that case the answer is NOTHING: this encoding does not say what I can recover.
DECLARE `What happened to me` IS ONE OF
    `my supply failed, was delayed, interrupted or restricted`                         -- s 27(2)
    `my supply was refused or cut off under s 21, 22 or 23`                            -- ss 21(5), 22(4), 23(3)
    `the Board reduced my supply because its water was insufficient`                   -- s 28
    `the Board's works interrupted or damaged my ways, watercourses or drains`         -- s 38(2)
    `I complied with a s 24A notice to move my apparatus or remove an object`          -- s 24A(7)
    `the Board entered my premises to survey, inspect or examine its pipes`            -- ss 24(1), 31(3)
    `the Board entered and occupied my premises to lay pipes or meters`                -- s 24A(2), Part 3A: not encoded

DECLARE `What I can recover` IS ONE OF
    `nothing: the Act excludes the Board's liability`
    `a proportionate abatement of the sum I agreed to pay for the supply`
    `reasonable compensation for my damage`
    `my costs and expenses reasonably incurred in complying`

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to me`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What I can recover`
DECIDE `What can I recover from the Board` IS
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `my supply failed, was delayed, interrupted or restricted` THEN JUST `nothing: the Act excludes the Board's liability`
    WHEN `my supply was refused or cut off under s 21, 22 or 23` THEN JUST `nothing: the Act excludes the Board's liability`
    WHEN `the Board reduced my supply because its water was insufficient` THEN JUST `a proportionate abatement of the sum I agreed to pay for the supply`
    WHEN `the Board's works interrupted or damaged my ways, watercourses or drains` THEN JUST `reasonable compensation for my damage`
    WHEN `I complied with a s 24A notice to move my apparatus or remove an object` THEN JUST `my costs and expenses reasonably incurred in complying`
    WHEN `the Board entered my premises to survey, inspect or examine its pipes` THEN JUST `nothing: the Act excludes the Board's liability`
    WHEN `the Board entered and occupied my premises to lay pipes or meters` THEN NOTHING   -- Part 3A not encoded

§§ `s 25 -- what may be done to my goods for an unpaid bill`

-- s 25(1): if a tax or moneys due for the supply of water to premises "owned or occupied by the person", for work or materials, or
-- for the hire of fittings, "is not paid within the time allowed", "a notice may be issued requiring the defaulter to pay the same,
-- together with a fee ... within 7 days from the date of the notice". (2): "If the amount and fee are not paid within the period of
-- 7 days, a warrant may be issued ... directing [an employee] to levy the same and the costs of recovery by seizure and sale of the
-- movable property of the defaulter." (3): the employee "may break open in the daytime any house or building" to seize.
-- (6): seized property is to be sold by public auction "at any time after the end of 7 days from the date of the seizure, unless in
-- the meantime the amount of the debt and the costs mentioned in the warrant have been paid". (7): the surplus "must be paid to the
-- owner of the property so sold". (8): "Any surplus remaining unclaimed for a period of 12 months from the date of the sale must be
-- paid to the credit of the Board's fund and no person thereafter is entitled to demand and receive it."
-- "within 7 days from the date of the notice" is read as excluding the day of the notice, so the 7th day after it is the last day
-- to pay (an inference: the Interpretation Act rule on computing time is not deposited).
GIVEN `the date of the demand notice` IS A DATE, `the date in question` IS A DATE, `I have paid the amount and the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a warrant issue to seize and sell my goods` IF
        DATE_SERIAL `the date in question` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the date of the demand notice` PLUS 7
    AND NOT `I have paid the amount and the fee`

GIVEN `the date of the seizure` IS A DATE, `the date in question` IS A DATE, `I have paid the debt and the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my seized goods be auctioned` IF
        DATE_SERIAL `the date in question` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the date of the seizure` PLUS 7
    AND NOT `I have paid the debt and the costs`

-- The same day n years on; 29 February in a year that has none is taken as 1 March (an inference: the text gives no rule).
GIVEN d IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary of` MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY d EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 2 AND NOT `leap`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 y
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) y
  WHERE
    y MEANS DATE_YEAR d PLUS n
    `leap` MEANS (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))) OR y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

-- "unclaimed for a period of 12 months from the date of the sale": a claim before the first anniversary of the sale is in time.
GIVEN `the date of the sale` IS A DATE, `the date I claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still claim the surplus from the sale of my goods` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the date I claim` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the anniversary of` `the date of the sale` 1)

§§ `ss 34, 37(1) -- the occupier's duties`

-- s 34(1): where a pipe or apparatus "placed in or upon any premises for the use or supply of water to the occupier ... becomes
-- obstructed or in any way damaged so as to cause a waste of water, the occupier must, immediately on the same coming to the
-- occupier's knowledge, give notice thereof to the Board". (2): neglect is an offence, "a fine not exceeding $5,000", and the supply
-- may be summarily discontinued.
GIVEN `the place` IS A `My place`
      `a pipe supplying me is obstructed or damaged so as to waste water` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I know of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I told the Board immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an offence by not reporting a wasting pipe` IF
        `Am I the occupier` `the place`
    AND `a pipe supplying me is obstructed or damaged so as to waste water`
    AND `I know of it`
    AND NOT `I told the Board immediately`

-- s 37(1): if, after the Board has discontinued the supply, "it is found that the supply has been reinstated without the authority
-- of the Board and the water is being used by any person on the premises, the occupier of the premises is deemed, until the contrary
-- is proved, to have authorised such user and shall be guilty of an offence": $10,000 and $250 a day continuing.
-- The burden is the occupier's: unless I prove I did not authorise the use, I am guilty.
GIVEN `the place` IS A `My place`
      `the Board discontinued the supply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supply was reinstated without the Board's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone on the premises is using the water` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I prove I did not authorise the use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty because the supply was reinstated without authority` IF
        `Am I the occupier` `the place`
    AND `the Board discontinued the supply`
    AND `the supply was reinstated without the Board's authority`
    AND `someone on the premises is using the water`
    AND NOT `I prove I did not authorise the use`

§§ `s 68B -- can I get back what I overpaid`

-- s 68B(1): "Except as provided in this section, a person is not entitled to a refund or return of any money that was overpaid or
-- erroneously paid ... as a fee or charge (including any price mentioned in section 20(1)) or tax under this Act". (3): a refund
-- "may be made only if -- (a) the person makes the claim within 5 years starting on the date of the overpayment, erroneous payment
-- or erroneous collection; (b) the claim is in the form and manner required by the Board; and (c) the Board is satisfied that there
-- was an overpayment, erroneous payment or erroneous collection".
-- "within 5 years starting on the date" is read as ending on the day before the fifth anniversary (an inference). The Board's
-- satisfaction is its judgment, asked as a fact; even when all three are met, the refund "may" be made.
DECLARE `Refund answer` IS ONE OF
    `a refund may be made`
    `no refund: the claim is out of time`
    `no refund: the claim is not in the form and manner the Board requires`
    `no refund: the Board is not satisfied there was an overpayment`

GIVEN `the date of the overpayment` IS A DATE
      `the date I claim` IS A DATE
      `my claim is in the form and manner the Board requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Board is satisfied there was an overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Refund answer`
DECIDE `Can I get my overpayment refunded` IS
    BRANCH
        IF DATE_SERIAL `the date I claim` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (`the anniversary of` `the date of the overpayment` 5)
            THEN `no refund: the claim is out of time`
        IF NOT `my claim is in the form and manner the Board requires`
            THEN `no refund: the claim is not in the form and manner the Board requires`
        IF NOT `the Board is satisfied there was an overpayment`
            THEN `no refund: the Board is not satisfied there was an overpayment`
        OTHERWISE `a refund may be made`
